          <h2>What is true</h2>
          <p>I was born in the United States. I later became a naturalized Peruvian citizen. I bought property before that, and I bought property after. I have lived in various parts of the country. I have bought and sold for a profit because I knew local price ranges. I am not publishing the prices, the profits, or the addresses. There is a <a href="cases.html">page waiting for those stories in my own words</a>, and it is labeled as waiting.</p>
          <p>I am not your lawyer, your notary, or your tax advisor. I do not present myself as a registered <span lang="es">agente inmobiliario</span>. The legal transaction is done with an independent <span lang="es">abogado</span> and an independent <span lang="es">notario</span>. [Placeholder: independent abogado and notario in the region. Names go here when I choose to publish them.]</p>
          <h2>What I do</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Help you decide what kind of life you are shopping for, including a rental first.</li>
            <li>Match climate, hospitals, and budget to places I can describe honestly.</li>
            <li>Search, including off-market, and compare a price with local ranges.</li>
            <li>Scout: photos, video, neighbors, boundaries, and the hours listings skip.</li>
            <li>Sit with you through the sequence and introduce the independent professionals.</li>
            <li>Afterward, caretaker check-ins and a clear eye on construction. Not a management company.</li>
          </ul>
          <h2>What I do not do</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Give legal, tax, immigration, or investment advice.</li>
            <li>Guarantee a title, a profit, a rental yield, or a visa. Buying property does not grant residency. Land values can fall.</li>
            <li>Claim I can walk every region of Peru. Other regions happen through a trusted local contact when that is the honest fit.</li>
            <li>Publish a commission policy. Fees are quoted for a stated service after intake.</li>
            <li>Remove squatters, pressure a neighbor, or “fix” a file that your lawyer says is bad.</li>
          </ul>
